heme.prompt:
Decide ONE question about one food, and nothing else.

The food: {{FOOD}}

WHAT THIS FOOD MOST LIKELY IS, with the confidence of each guess: {{IDENTITY}}. These are given to you — judge by them and do not re-guess the species yourself.

THE CATEGORIES OF RICH HEME-IRON SOURCES:
— LIVER itself — of any animal, bird or fish — and food made mainly of liver: pâté, liver sausage, liver cake;
— OTHER INNER ORGANS themselves — hearts, kidneys, tongues, gizzards, lungs, blood sausage — of any animal, bird or fish. It is the ORGAN that belongs to this category, never the animal's flesh: a fish fillet, a bird's breast or leg is not an organ;
— MEAT OF MAMMALS: beef, veal, pork, lamb, mutton, goat, and the meat of other farmed or wild mammals — venison, elk, boar, horse, rabbit — in any cut, ground or whole, raw or cooked, and food made mainly of such meat: sausage, frankfurters, ham, bacon, salami, mince, meatballs, cutlets, stew, canned meat. A creature that is not a mammal has no meat in this category;
— MOLLUSCS OF THESE KINDS ONLY: mussels, oysters, clams and vongole, cockles, octopus, whelks, winkles. The category is these kinds, not the zoological class: a mollusc of another kind does not belong to it.

Do not reason about how many milligrams of iron a food holds — you do not know those numbers, and the categories already account for them.

A composite dish belongs to a category only when such an ingredient is its MAIN part. Words about preparation, storage, freezing, packaging, cut, grade or country of origin never change what a food is.

Fill the reason field FIRST — name the ONE category that fits, or say that none does — and let the verdict follow from it. Never list the categories that do not fit: running through them turns into denying them all, the right one included.

Respond with ONLY a single minified JSON object with the fields from the schema.

fat_composite.prompt:
Our automatic classifier says this product is: {{IDENTITY}}

Is this a DISH COOKED FROM SEVERAL DIFFERENT FOODS, or is it a SINGLE food?

A SINGLE FOOD is one food, however processed. These count as one:
— the flesh, organs, fat or skin of one animal, bird or fish, raw or cooked;
— one plant and what is pressed or ground from it: an oil, a nut, a seed, a grain, a vegetable, a fruit;
— milk and everything made from milk alone: butter, cream, cheese, curd, yoghurt;
— eggs;
— a factory product built around one of these: sausage, ham, tinned fish, nut paste.

A DISH is cooked from several foods at once: stuffed vegetables, cabbage rolls, cutlets and meatballs, casseroles and bakes, pies and pastry with a filling, pilaf, stews and soups, salads with dressing, sandwiches, waffles, ready meals.

A dish stays a dish even when one of its foods plainly outweighs the rest: борщ with beef is cooked from meat, vegetables and the oil they were fried in, and that makes it a dish. Do not ask which part is the largest — ask whether more than one food went into it.

Fill the reason FIRST — name what this food is made of — and let the verdict follow from it.

Respond with ONLY a single minified JSON object.
